## ===========================================================================
## BOBBY AND MAIDEN HOUSE — Book 6 (`story.ni:5603-5803`) and Book 5
## (`story.ni:5804-6549`), Chapter 3.
##
## The change document ("Chapter 3 — Bobby and Maiden House", 2026-09-01)
## authorizes Books 6 and 5 in file order, ending as Jack climbs out through
## the privy window: the coin trick and Bobby in the Back Alley, the
## courtyard and the door, the curfew that turns the world to night and locks
## her in, the widows in their rooms, sleep in the dormitory, and the window.
## Every line is Gentry's; conversations are STUBS under the standing rule.
##
## NIGHT. The source's curfew "sets the scene for night" (`story.ni:5937`):
## the port carries the hour as `Toresal`, an offstage entity whose state
## every later clause can read (`while Toresal is night`). The market's night
## remap and Bobby's move to the night market are Chapter 4's.
##
## THE NEW SCENE (change document, "Pressure", David 2026-09-01): a mercenary
## comes to the Maiden House door in the night; Theresa holds the door; he
## leaves saying "I'll be back!"; it is what wakes Jack, and she waits Theresa
## out before slipping from her bunk. Built as the trigger at the source's
## waking point (the bunk passage, `story.ni:5985`) with ONE placeholder — the
## knock, both voices, the parting word, and the wait are David's lines. The
## wait is narrated inside the placeholder, not spent as turns (the gap the
## change document left to this build — reported, David's to redirect).
##
## STUBS TAKING THE SOURCE'S PATH (flagged, per the standing rule's item 4):
## Bobby's alley tree — `talk to bobby` prints the BO11 TODO, and Bobby leaves
## as `BO10` ("I'm in") would have him leave; before that, the alley's exits
## refuse with the BO7/"in or out" TODO. Fiona's "concerned for our safety"
## hold (`FI3`..`FI7`) never arms, because the quips that arm it are stubbed;
## the kitchen door is open. Dame Sandler's DS14 precedent applies.
##
## THE RAID (Chapter 7, `gallows.chord`) is layered on below, gated on
## `the raid`'s states: the Dormitory held at the bedside, the Hallway's
## exits during the pounding and after the expulsion, the front door's
## refusals, the Laundry's gap north, the widows' talk and the letter, the
## window's second climb (Chapter VIII's row). Bobby's and Shannon's idles
## and the widows' presence lines end with the hanging (`before gallows`).
##
## Not carried, noted: kissing refusals (no action); `in`/`out` as door
## directions; the wooden door as a Chord door — it is scenery on each side
## and the Hallway's north exit is blocked at night, because the door must
## LOCK at runtime and only the blocked exit says so; the source's
## `[if location is the Privy]` in the window's `search` text reads inverted
## in the source and is carried as written; the widows' words for Jack
## outside the trees (the curfew passage, Theresa's sneer, Fiona's "young
## lady", Shannon's goodbye) are carried as the source has them — David's to
## convert under §3g (comments mark each).
## ===========================================================================

## The hour. Day until the curfew; every later chapter reads it.

create Toresal
  aka the city, the hour
  proper
  states, reversible: day, night

  The city of Toresal.

