## `story.ni:5627`, verbatim, the first entry.

define phrase coin-trick
  At the end of the alley, a group of young urchins — none older than their
  eighth year — are clustered around something. As you draw closer, you see
  Bobby crouched in the midst of them. He's holding his arm out, his fist
  loosely clenched in front of a dirty-cheeked child of six.

  'Go on,' says Bobby. 'Go on, take a look.'

  The little boy, his eyes wide and solemn, reaches out and pries Bobby's
  fingers open. His hand is empty. The little boy looks dismayed.

  'Ah, but what's this?' asks Bobby. And he reaches forward and draws a copper
  coin from behind the boy's grimy ear. There is a collective gasp and squeals
  of delight from the rest of the children. The little boy's eyes look ready
  to fall out of his head.

  Bobby presses the coin into the little boy's hand, then passes out more
  coins to the others. 'Here,' he says, 'keep it safe in your pocket. Spend it
  on bread, not candy.' The children take their prizes and scatter.
end phrase

## Bobby does not perceive Jack (change document, "Who sees her"; the source
## says so in his description). `proposing` until the tree's "I'm in";
## `agreed` after, when he has gone to wait for her.

define trait kick-bobby
  on the player kicking
    refuse bobby-never-hurt
  end on
end trait

create Bobby
  aka bobby, lad, boy, handsome lad
  a person, proper
  pronouns he
  kick-bobby
  states: proposing, agreed, leading, returning, gone

  Bobby is a few years older than you, a tall, broad-shouldered lad with
  tousled black hair and a rakish grin. He's an orphan, like you, and like you
  he makes the streets of the city his home and lives by his wits. Unlike you,
  he doesn't have the safety net of Maiden House to fall back on, but somehow
  he always seems to do well for himself.

  You also happen to think that he's devastatingly handsome, although you
  would never admit that under the worst torture the King's interrogators
  could devise. He doesn't even know that you're really a girl, and you're not
  about to tell him, because if he knew he would certainly stop inviting you
  along on his exploits.

  on every turn while Bobby is here and one chance in 5 and the player is not in the Secret Way and before gallows
    phrase bobby-idle
  end on

  on the player attacking
    refuse bobby-never-hurt
  end on

  when the player's dawdle expires
    move Bobby here
    phrase dawdle-hide-stub
    move Bobby to the Pasture when the player is in the Lord's Road
    move Bobby to the Stream Crossing when the player is in the Pasture
    move Bobby to the Clearing when the player is in the Stream Crossing
    move Bobby to the Lord's Road when Bobby is here
  end when

  on the player talking
    refuse when the hanging is speaking: cant-reach-him
    phrase bobby-finger-to-lips when the player is in the Lord's Keep
    phrase bobby-not-now when the player is in the Tunnels
    phrase bobby-bo27-stub when Bobby is leading and the player is in the Clearing
    move the player to the Underneath the Fountain when Bobby is leading and the player is in the Clearing
    phrase bobby-bo26-stub when Bobby is agreed and the player is in the Market Square
    move Bobby to the Lord's Road when Bobby is agreed and the player is in the Market Square
    start the player's dawdle when Bobby is agreed and the player is in the Market Square
    change Bobby to leading when Bobby is agreed and the player is in the Market Square
    phrase bobby-bo11-stub when Bobby is proposing
    move Bobby offstage when Bobby is proposing
    change Bobby to agreed when Bobby is proposing
  end on

## `ATMOS_Bobby` (`story.ni:5662`), plain every-turn texture (P-9).

define phrase bobby-idle, randomly
  Bobby whistles a few notes of some popular mummer's tune.
or
  Bobby smirks at you in that way he has, that makes you want to smile and
  blush and run and hide, all at the same time.
or
  You realize you're staring, and quickly find something else to look at.
  Goddesses, but he's handsome.
or
  Bobby rakes his fingers back through his tangled hair.
end phrase

define phrase bobby-never-hurt
  You'd never dream of hurting Bobby!
end phrase

