end phrase

define phrase dishes-dried
  You take one of the wet dishes from the basin, dry it, and place it on the
  'clean' stack.

  Fiona smiles at you. 'Thank you, dear.'
end phrase

define phrase dishes-continue
  You continue helping with the dishes, drying and stacking.
end phrase

define phrase pans-leave-alone
  You're not about to cook anything and they don't need cleaning, so you might
  as well leave the pots and pans alone.
end phrase

define phrase ceiling-too-high
  The ceiling is low, but it's still higher than you can reach.
end phrase

define phrase dishwater-nasty
  No thanks; that stuff looks nasty.
end phrase

