define phrase fiona-idle, randomly
  Widow Fiona grunts as she leans over the basin's edge to dunk another
  gravy-encrusted plate into the soapy water.
or
  Widow Fiona wipes a plate dry on her apron and stacks it on the counter.
or
  Widow Fiona inspects a plate closely, and scrapes at a bit of stuck food
  with her thumbnail.
or
  Widow Fiona inspects a plate closely, then stacks it on the counter.
or
  Widow Fiona inspects a plate closely, then dunks it back into the basin.
or
  Widow Fiona gives you a broad, rosy-cheeked smile.
end phrase

