define phrase tub-no-bath
  You don't need a bath right now. And you definitely don't need a bath in
  that.
end phrase

define phrase water-steeping
  The grimy underpants of two dozen hygiene-challenged urchins have been
  steeping in that water all day.
end phrase

define phrase laundry-leave-alone
  Better leave the clothes alone. They're in that tub for a reason.
end phrase

define phrase clothes-someone-naked
  If you took those clothes, someone in Maiden House would end up having to go
  naked. You can't have that on your conscience.
end phrase

## Shannon SEES her (vision.md §4): "Jacqueline" is the tell and stays.

create Widow Shannon
  aka shannon, widow, maiden, young widow, plain woman
  a person, proper
  pronouns she
  in the Laundry

  Shannon is the youngest of the widows in Maiden House. She is plain-looking,
  none too bright, and, to all appearances, utterly uninterested in ever
  remarrying, which is perhaps just as well. She devotes herself to the
  children, particularly the toddlers, and does most of the cleaning and
  cooking for Maiden House.

  on every turn while Widow Shannon is here and one chance in 4 and before gallows
    phrase shannon-idle
  end on

  on the player talking
    refuse when the raid is pounding: shannon-get-inside
    refuse when the raid is aftermath: shannon-talk-later
    refuse when the raid is keyed: shannon-talk-later
    refuse when the player is in the Duke's House: reluctant-to-break-silence
    refuse when the company is escorting: shannon-sh13-stub
    refuse shannon-sh1-stub
  end on

  when Jack moves, while the company is escorting
    move Widow Shannon here
  end when

