## `ATMOS_Shannon_Laundry` (`story.ni:6437`), plain texture (P-9).

define phrase shannon-idle, randomly
  Widow Shannon picks up a thick wooden stick and jabs at the clothes soaking
  in the tub, stirring them about.
or
  Widow Shannon steps back from the tub for a moment, wiping the sweat off her
  brow.
or
  Widow Shannon pulls a shirt from the grayish water, wrings it out, and hangs
  it up on the line behind her.
or
  Widow Shannon pulls a shift from the grayish water, wrings it out, and hangs
  it up on the line behind her.
or
  Widow Shannon pulls a pair of trousers from the grayish water, wrings it
  out, and hangs it up on the line behind her.
or
  Widow Shannon pulls a diaper from the grayish water, wrings it out, and
  hangs it up on the line behind her.
or
  Widow Shannon pulls a sock from the grayish water, wrings it out, and hangs
  it up on the line behind her.
or
  Widow Shannon gives you a friendly nod.
end phrase

